      "claim": "Direct human absolute oral bioavailability measurements in the most transferable benzimidazole/heteroaryl-morpholine contexts are all at or above 20%, mostly 40-90%: abemaciclib 43-49%, mizolastine 65-70%, doxazosin 62-75%, abecarnil 29-96%, compound 5 41%, and gefitinib ~60%.",
      "card_ids": ["C01","C07","C11","C15","C24","C29","C04","C13","C20","C30","C42","C02","C06","C21","C23","C32","C39","C08","C14","C17","C10"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 solubility records for ionizable heteroaromatic/morpholine-containing analogs show moderate-to-high aqueous solubility (imatinib very soluble across pH 1-7.5; gefitinib 2.6-0.17 mg/mL at pH 4-5; KR-69232 122 µg/mL; compound 21i 40 µg/mL in PBS pH 7), indicating the query's ionizable morpholine/pyrazole/amidine groups are unlikely to be solubility-limited.",
      "card_ids": ["C143","C133","C159","C147","C174"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 permeability records for heteroaromatic/pyrazole/morpholine-containing compounds are moderate, not clearly low (DMP-851 Papp 5.2×10^-6 cm/s; acidic tetrazole Papp 2.9; morpholine-containing compound 3 Papp 2.0), so L4 provides no affirmative evidence of F < 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C160","C158","C152"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Low aqueous solubility of neutral benzimidazoles (mebendazole, flubendazole, carbendazim) is not transferable to the query because the query carries ionizable solubilizing groups (morpholine, N-hydroxyamidine, pyrazole) and has computed logD 0.53/neutral fraction 0.02.",
      "card_ids": ["C155","C139","C154","C165"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "An L3 oral/IV radioactivity AUC comparison in rats for a benzimidazole-containing compound (BPA) showed oral AUC 102 vs IV 118 ng-eq·h/mL (~86%), consistent with high oral exposure for a benzimidazole-containing scaffold.",
      "card_ids": ["C118"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "intestinal_absorption_permeability",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": ["C143","C133","C159","C147","C174","C160","C158","C152","C155","C139","C154","C165"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct query-specific absolute oral bioavailability, AUC, Cmax, or IV-comparison measurement.",
    "No query-specific permeability (Caco-2/MDCK/PAMPA) or intestinal absorption measurement; L4 records are for analogs with moderate transferability.",
    "The unique N-hydroxycyclopropylamidine (isourea) moiety is not represented in any L1-L4 context; its effect on absorption, stability, and first-pass is unknown.",
    "Computed low neutral fraction (0.02), low logD (0.53), and high TPSA (114.45) remain unvalidated experimentally; formulation, dose, and solubility effects are unknown.",
    "No gut-wall efflux or intestinal-metabolism data yet (L5 pending)."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high (F >= 20%) maintained and modestly strengthened: L1 direct human F measurements in related benzimidazole/heteroaryl-morpholine contexts are all >=20% (mostly 40-90%), L3 oral exposure records show substantial AUC/Cmax, and L4 solubility/permeability records for ionizable analogs indicate adequate solubility and moderate permeability with no affirmative sub-threshold evidence; the unfavorable computed ionization prior is not endpoint proof, and residual uncertainty from the unique isourea moiety and lack of query-specific data is captured in moderate confidence."
}

